<title>JAPAN: Dlr-yen rate of 105-115 appropriate -- Suzuki Motor.</title>
<headline>Dlr-yen rate of 105-115 appropriate -- Suzuki Motor.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Suzuki Motor Corp president Osamu Suzuki told a news conference on Tuesday that a dollar yen rate of 105-115 yen was an appropriate level for Japanese companies.  </p>
<p>Suzuki said the current weaker yen would have almost no impact on the firm's earnings this fiscal year to March 31 because almost all its exports were yen-denominated.</p>
<p>He said dollar-denominated exports accounted for only three percent of the firm's overall exports in 1996/97 against 15 percent in the past.</p>
</text>
